                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "16040b6d-cd54-392d-b0d0-9a070505767d",
                        "entry_id": "cc3eed71-a31d-36a3-80c4-eb557b14bb10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various historical medicines, typically an electuary compounded with various poison, believed to derive from Mithridates VI and to serve as a universal antidote."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "historical",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b699e376-54d7-4df0-8a8a-03db39b523da",
                                "sense_id": "16040b6d-cd54-392d-b0d0-9a070505767d",
                                "text": "Auicen saythe; There be certeyne medicins... which wyl not suffre poyson to approche nere the harte, as triacle and Metridate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8397e2c3-3004-4c55-835f-1f0099034fe1",
                                "sense_id": "16040b6d-cd54-392d-b0d0-9a070505767d",
                                "text": "After I had thus evacuated the Plethora, and diſpoſed her body for Mercurialls more operative, I gave her each morning and evening a few grains of Mercur. diaphoret. in a bolus with conſ. lujule and Mithridate [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c273bb2-199a-4eeb-b62f-5ef260fd83b8",
                                "sense_id": "16040b6d-cd54-392d-b0d0-9a070505767d",
                                "text": "Fools may talk of Mythridate, Cordials, Elixers..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ad11db9-8dc9-4cfb-909a-b1077840d6ee",
                                "sense_id": "16040b6d-cd54-392d-b0d0-9a070505767d",
                                "text": "What he wanted, in effect, was a universal antidote, which medical science has for years referred to as a mithridate."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cfd948c-e17b-3dbf-9eb9-2c085b822e50",
                        "entry_id": "cc3eed71-a31d-36a3-80c4-eb557b14bb10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various historical medicines, typically an electuary compounded with various poison, believed to derive from Mithridates VI and to serve as a universal antidote.",
                            "Synonym of cure."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "broadly",
                            "countable",
                            "figuratively",
                            "historical",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4892261-6a83-46d7-b609-732f5a1fe27d",
                                "sense_id": "1cfd948c-e17b-3dbf-9eb9-2c085b822e50",
                                "text": "The contemplation was a mithridate to a pestered conceipted minde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fdd85bb-98a7-43ac-86fc-2ac712d78e0f",
                                "sense_id": "1cfd948c-e17b-3dbf-9eb9-2c085b822e50",
                                "text": "That which maketh me most both to sorrow and wonder, is that musick (a methridat for melancholy) should make him mad."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f531d700-cf9b-384e-b69f-3f72dda792ef",
                        "entry_id": "cc3eed71-a31d-36a3-80c4-eb557b14bb10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of mithridate mustard."
                        ],
